exclude(2016,3,3.5,'No. At a fixed x, order the four values a≤b≤c≤d. If b+c>0, all pair sums among b,c,d are positive; if b+c<0, all pair sums among a,b,c are negative. Each polynomial pair sum keeps its sign on the real line because it has no root. Thus that triple sum, half the sum of its three pair sums, can never vanish.')
